      "html": "<p>Quickler captures the self-evaluation walk and the evidence: photos of your setting and outdoor space, your observations against each quality indicator, your safety and premises checks, the state of your policies and certificates at the point of check. It keeps a permanent, searchable record you can show at a visit.</p><p>It is not a children's records system, a learning journal, an attendance register or a child protection case-management system. It does not hold personal plans, developmental records, attendance or any child's personal information. When self-evaluation needs to check that a child's records are in order, you record the finding, that they were reviewed and were current and child-centred or not, without copying anyone's data into quickler. Those records stay in your own systems as the single source of truth. Quickler is the evaluation and evidence layer around them. It records that a check was done and captures the evidence; it is not a child protection case-management system. Quickler is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Care Inspectorate, and whether your evidence satisfies an inspection is a judgement for you and your inspector.</p>"
