      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What is childminder self-evaluation in Scotland?</h3><p>It is the process by which a Scottish childminder judges their own service against the Care Inspectorate's quality framework and the Health and Social Care Standards, honestly and continuously, and evidences each judgement. It covers care, play and learning, your setting, you as the person providing the care including safeguarding, and how you lead and improve your service, graded on a six-point scale. Childminding in Scotland is regulated by the Care Inspectorate, not Ofsted, which covers England only, and not CQC.</p><h3>What childminder record keeping does the Care Inspectorate expect?</h3><p>The Care Inspectorate expects a childminder to keep the records that evidence safe, high-quality care and their own self-evaluation: safety and premises checks, risk assessments, policies, training and certificates, and an honest, current self-evaluation and improvement plan. Personal records about children, such as personal plans and attendance, are kept in your own systems. Quickler captures the self-evaluation and evidence side, not the children's personal records. Always work from the current published framework, as the Care Inspectorate updates its guidance, and treat this as general information, not regulatory advice.</p><h3>How does a childminder Care Inspectorate inspection work?</h3><p>The Care Inspectorate inspects against its quality framework and the Health and Social Care Standards, grades key questions on a six-point scale from unsatisfactory to excellent, and looks at how honestly you self-evaluate and act on what you find. A childminder who knows their service, evidences their judgements and can show live improvement work fares better than one writing a self-evaluation the night before. Quickler is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Care Inspectorate, and whether your evidence satisfies an inspection is a judgement for you and your inspector.</p><h3>Can I run childminder self-evaluation over WhatsApp, and what does it cost?</h3><p>Yes. Quickler's workflow runs over the WhatsApp Business API. You receive each prompt in your existing WhatsApp chat and reply with text, a voice note or a photo against each quality indicator, and the report and improvement plan generate automatically. No separate app or login is required, and no child's personal data is entered, because quickler is an audit and evidence tool, not a children's records or child protection system. There is a free tier of 20 reports a month and up to 10 photos per report, which usually suits a single childminder well, with no card and no trial clock. Beyond that, quickler is £20 per active user a month, where an active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, with a £20 minimum, and dormant users are free.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/nursery-self-evaluation-scotland.html\">Nursery self-evaluation Scotland</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-self-evaluation-scotland.html\">Care Inspectorate self-evaluation Scotland</a></li></ul>"
