  "seoBody": "<h2>Childminder self-evaluation in Scotland</h2><p>In Scotland, childminders are regulated by the Care Inspectorate. Ofsted regulates childcare in England; in Scotland it is the Care Inspectorate, and it is not CQC either. A childminder self-evaluates and is inspected against the Health and Social Care Standards and the Care Inspectorate's quality framework for childminding and early learning and childcare, graded on a six-point scale from unsatisfactory to excellent.</p><p>Self-evaluation is not a one-off form. It is an expectation that you reflect on your own practice continuously, judge your service honestly against the quality indicators, and evidence each judgement. An honest self-evaluation finds the gaps an inspector would find, while there is time to close them. It does not raise the grade on its own. Acting on it does.</p><h2>Record-keeping when it is just you</h2><p>A childminder is the practitioner, the manager and the person who keeps the paperwork, usually while minding children. That is why record-keeping slips: there is no quiet office moment. Capturing on your phone at the point of the check fixes it. The garden gate, the smoke alarm, the outing risk assessment: a quick message, a photo or a voice note, and the evidence exists with a date attached.</p><p>Quickler keeps a permanent, searchable record you build as you go, and turns each finding into an action with a date, so your improvement plan stays live rather than being rewritten before each visit.</p><h2>What quickler captures, and where it stops</h2><p>The honest boundary: quickler is an audit and self-evaluation and evidence tool. It is not a children's records system, a learning journal, an attendance register or a child protection case-management system. It records that a check was done and captures the evidence, without holding any child's personal information. Those records stay in your own systems as the single source of truth. Quickler is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Care Inspectorate, and whether your evidence satisfies an inspection is a judgement for you and your inspector. Treat this page as general information, not regulatory advice, and always work from the current published framework and standards.</p><h2>Pricing for a sole childminder</h2><p>For a childminder working alone, the free tier is usually plenty: 20 reports a month and up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock. Beyond that, pricing is only for active users: [[price:bundles]]. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, with a £20 minimum, and dormant users are free.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/nursery-self-evaluation-scotland.html\">Nursery self-evaluation Scotland</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-self-evaluation-scotland.html\">Care Inspectorate self-evaluation Scotland</a></li></ul>",
